{"id":"translator-and-historical-edition-notes-part-5","label":"Translator and historical edition notes (part 5)","headingNoteRefs":"","context":"","kind":"commentary","blocks":[{"text":"[^n1715]: Luke ix. 38a; Matt. xvii. 14b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1715"},{"text":"[^n1716]: Luke ix. 38b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1716"},{"text":"[^n1717]: Luke ix. 39a; Matt. xvii. 15b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1717"},{"text":"[^n1718]: Lit. The son-of-the-roof, a Syriac phrase meaning a demon of lunacy.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1718"},{"text":"[^n1719]: Mark ix. 18a.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1719"},{"text":"[^n1720]: A word used in Arabic of the devil producing insanity; but here it reproduces the Peshitta.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1720"},{"text":"[^n1721]: Lit. becometh light; but a comparison with the Peshitta suggests that we should change one diacritical point and read withereth, as in Ibn-at-Tayyib’s Commentary. An equally easy emendation would be wasteth.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1721"},{"text":"[^n1722]: Matt. xvii. 15c; Luke ix. 39c.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1722"},{"text":"[^n1723]: Matt. xvii. 16.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1723"},{"text":"[^n1724]: Matt. xvii. 17.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1724"},{"text":"[^n1725]: Mark ix. 20.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1725"},{"text":"[^n1726]: Mark ix. 21.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1726"},{"text":"[^n1727]: Mark ix. 22b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1727"},{"text":"[^n1728]: Mark ix. 23.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1728"},{"text":"[^n1729]: Mark ix. 24.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1729"},{"text":"[^n1730]: Mark ix. 25.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1730"},{"text":"[^n1731]: In Syriac, but not in Arabic, the word means deaf or dumb, according to the context.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1731"},{"text":"[^n1732]: Ciasca’s Arabic follows Vat. ms. in inserting a that (pronoun) after thee.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1732"},{"text":"[^n1733]: Mark ix. 26.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1733"},{"text":"[^n1734]: Doubtless alternative renderings of the same Syriac word (demon).","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1734"},{"text":"[^n1735]: Mark ix. 27a; Luke ix. 42b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1735"},{"text":"[^n1736]: Matt. xvii. 18b; Luke ix. 43a.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1736"},{"text":"[^n1737]: Mark ix. 28.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1737"},{"text":"[^n1738]: Lit. between themselves and him.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1738"},{"text":"[^n1739]: Matt. xvii. 20.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1739"},{"text":"[^n1740]: Mark ix. 29b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1740"},{"text":"[^n1741]: Mark ix. 30.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1741"},{"text":"[^n1742]: Or, about him.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1742"},{"text":"[^n1743]: Mark ix. 31a; Luke ix. 44a.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1743"},{"text":"[^n1744]: Mark ix. 31b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1744"},{"text":"[^n1745]: Luke ix. 45.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1745"},{"text":"[^n1746]: Matt. xvii. 23b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1746"},{"text":"[^n1747]: Luke ix. 46.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1747"},{"text":"[^n1748]: Borg. ms. omits among them.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1748"},{"text":"[^n1749]: Mark ix. 33.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1749"},{"text":"[^n1750]: Mark ix. 34a.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1750"},{"text":"[^n1751]: Matt. xvii. 24b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1751"},{"text":"[^n1752]: Matt. xvii. 25.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1752"},{"text":"[^n1753]: Matt. xvii. 26.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1753"},{"text":"[^n1754]: Matt. xvii. 27.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1754"},{"text":"[^n1755]: Matt. xviii. 1.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1755"},{"text":"[^n1756]: Luke ix. 47a; Mark ix. 36.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1756"},{"text":"[^n1757]: Lit. one (Syriac idiom).","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1757"},{"text":"[^n1758]: Matt. xviii. 3.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1758"},{"text":"[^n1759]: Luke ix. 48.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1759"},{"text":"[^n1760]: Mark ix. 37b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1760"},{"text":"[^n1761]: Luke ix. 48c.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1761"},{"text":"[^n1762]: In the present work this word frequently means synagogue.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1762"},{"text":"[^n1763]: Matt. xviii. 6.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1763"},{"text":"[^n1764]: Lit. millstone of an ass.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1764"},{"text":"[^n1765]: Luke ix. 49.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1765"},{"text":"[^n1766]: Mark ix. 39.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1766"},{"text":"[^n1767]: Luke ix. 50b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1767"},{"text":"[^n1768]: Matt. xviii. 7a, c.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1768"},{"text":"[^n1769]: i.e., experiences that test one; or, seductions. The word is variously used.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1769"},{"text":"[^n1770]: Matt. xviii. 8.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1770"},{"text":"[^n1771]: Or, is kindled.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1771"},{"text":"[^n1772]: Mark ix. 44.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1772"},{"text":"[^n1773]: Matt. xviii. 9a.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1773"},{"text":"[^n1774]: See note to § 25, 17.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1774"},{"text":"[^n1775]: Mark ix. 47b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1775"},{"text":"[^n1776]: Mark ix. 48.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1776"},{"text":"[^n1777]: Mark ix. 49.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1777"},{"text":"[^n1778]: Mark ix. 50a.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1778"},{"text":"[^n1779]: Luke xiv. 34b; Luke xiv. 35.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1779"},{"text":"[^n1780]: Mark ix. 50c.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1780"},{"text":"[^n1781]: Mark x. 1.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1781"},{"text":"[^n1782]: Mark x. 2.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1782"},{"text":"[^n1783]: Mark x. 3.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1783"},{"text":"[^n1784]: Mark x. 4.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1784"},{"text":"[^n1785]: Mark x. 5a.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1785"},{"text":"[^n1786]: Matt. xix. 4.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1786"},{"text":"[^n1787]: Matt. xix. 5.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1787"},{"text":"[^n1788]: Matt. xix. 6.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1788"},{"text":"[^n1789]: Matt. xix. 7.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1789"},{"text":"[^n1790]: So the Arabic; but the Syriac versions follow the Greek, and consent is doubtless a (very easy, and, in view of the succeeding context, natural) clerical error for an original Arabic charge.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1790"},{"text":"[^n1791]: Matt. xix. 8.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1791"},{"text":"[^n1792]: Matt. xix. 9a.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1792"},{"text":"[^n1793]: Or, leaveth.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1793"},{"text":"[^n1794]: Mark x. 10.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1794"},{"text":"[^n1795]: Mark x. 11.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1795"},{"text":"[^n1796]: Mark x. 12.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1796"},{"text":"[^n1797]: Matt. xix. 9b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1797"},{"text":"[^n1798]: Matt. xix. 10.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1798"},{"text":"[^n1799]: Lit. blame, a mistranslation (found also in the Brit. Mus. text of Ibn-at-Tayyib’s Commentary) of the Syriac word, which is ambiguous (cf. even the Greek). For a somewhat similar case see § 50, 11, note.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1799"},{"text":"[^n1800]: Matt. xix. 11.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1800"},{"text":"[^n1801]: Matt. xix. 12.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1801"},{"text":"[^n1802]: Lit. wombs.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1802"},{"text":"[^n1803]: Matt. xix. 13a.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1803"},{"text":"[^n1804]: Mark x. 13b; Mark x. 14.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1804"},{"text":"[^n1805]: Mark x. 15.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1805"},{"text":"[^n1806]: Mark x. 16.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1806"},{"text":"[^n1807]: Luke xv. 1.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1807"},{"text":"[^n1808]: Luke xv. 2.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1808"},{"text":"[^n1809]: Luke xv. 3.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1809"},{"text":"[^n1810]: Luke xv. 4.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1810"},{"text":"[^n1811]: Matt. xviii. 13.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1811"},{"text":"[^n1812]: Luke xv. 5b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1812"},{"text":"[^n1813]: Luke xv. 6.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1813"},{"text":"[^n1814]: Matt. xviii. 14.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1814"},{"text":"[^n1815]: Strictly, preferreth, but used also as in the text.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1815"},{"text":"[^n1816]: Luke xv. 7.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1816"},{"text":"[^n1817]: Luke xv. 8.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1817"},{"text":"[^n1818]: Luke xv. 9.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1818"},{"text":"[^n1819]: Luke xv. 10.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1819"},{"text":"[^n1820]: Luke xv. 11.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1820"},{"text":"[^n1821]: Luke xv. 12.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1821"},{"text":"[^n1822]: Luke xv. 13.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1822"},{"text":"[^n1823]: Luke xv. 14.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1823"},{"text":"[^n1824]: Luke xv. 15.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1824"},{"text":"[^n1825]: This word is regularly used throughout this work in this sense.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1825"},{"text":"[^n1826]: Luke xv. 16.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1826"},{"text":"[^n1827]: Luke xv. 17.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1827"},{"text":"[^n1828]: Luke xv. 18.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1828"},{"text":"[^n1829]: Luke xv. 19.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1829"},{"text":"[^n1830]: Luke xv. 20.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1830"},{"text":"[^n1831]: See above, § 24, 26, note.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n1831"},{"text":"[^n1832]: Did not Ibn-at-Tayyib’s Commentary (Brit. Mus. text) also read breast, we might assume it to be a clerical error fo